NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007470 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007471 "=head1 LIMITATIONS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007472 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007473 "The following limits are imposed by Excel 2007+:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007474 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007475 "    Description                                Limit"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007476 "    --------------------------------------     ------"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007477 "    Maximum number of chars in a string        32,767"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007478 "    Maximum number of columns                  16,384"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007479 "    Maximum number of rows                     1,048,576"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007480 "    Maximum chars in a sheet name              31"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007481 "    Maximum chars in a header/footer           254"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007482 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007483 "    Maximum characters in hyperlink url (1)    2079"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007484 "    Maximum number of unique hyperlinks (2)    65,530"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007485 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007486 "(1) Versions of Excel prior to Excel 2015 limited hyperlink links and anchor/locations to 255 characters each. Versions after that support urls up to 2079 characters. Excel::Writer::XLSX versions >= 1.0.2 support the new longer limit by default."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007487 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007488 "(2) Per worksheet. Excel allows a greater number of non-unique hyperlinks if they are contiguous and can be grouped into a single range. This isn't supported by Excel::Writer::XLSX."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007489 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007490 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007491 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007492 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007493 "=head1 REQUIREMENTS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007494 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007495 "L<http://search.cpan.org/search?dist=Archive-Zip/>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007496 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007497 "Perl 5.8.2."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007498 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007499 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007500 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007501 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007502 "=head1 SPEED AND MEMORY USAGE"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007503 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007504 "C<Spreadsheet::WriteExcel> was written to optimise speed and reduce memory usage. However, these design goals meant that it wasn't easy to implement features that many users requested such as writing formatting and data separately."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007505 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007506 "As a result C<Excel::Writer::XLSX> takes a different design approach and holds a lot more data in memory so that it is functionally more flexible."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007507 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007508 "The effect of this is that Excel::Writer::XLSX is about 30% slower than Spreadsheet::WriteExcel and uses 5 times more memory."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007509 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007510 "In addition the extended row and column ranges in Excel 2007+ mean that it is possible to run out of memory creating large files. This was almost never an issue with Spreadsheet::WriteExcel."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007511 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007512 "This memory usage can be reduced almost completely by using the Workbook C<set_optimization()> method:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007513 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007514 "    $workbook->set_optimization();"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007515 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007516 "The trade-off is that you won't be able to take advantage of features that manipulate cell data after it is written. One such feature is Tables."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007517 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007518 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007519 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007520 "=head1 DOWNLOADING"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007521 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007522 "The latest version of this module is always available at: L<http://search.cpan.org/search?dist=Excel-Writer-XLSX/>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007523 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007524 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007525 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007526 "=head1 INSTALLATION"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007527 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007528 "The module can be installed using the standard Perl procedure:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007529 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007530 "            perl Makefile.PL"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007531 "            make"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007532 "            make test"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007533 "            make install    # You may need to be sudo/root"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007534 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007535 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007536 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007537 "=head1 DIAGNOSTICS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007538 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007539 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007540 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007541 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007542 "=item Filename required by Excel::Writer::XLSX->new()"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007543 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007544 "A filename must be given in the constructor."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007545 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007546 "=item Can't open filename. It may be in use or protected."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007547 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007548 "The file cannot be opened for writing. The directory that you are writing to may be protected or the file may be in use by another program."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007549 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007550 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007551 "=item Can't call method \"XXX\" on an undefined value at someprogram.pl."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007552 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007553 "On Windows this is usually caused by the file that you are trying to create clashing with a version that is already open and locked by Excel."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007554 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007555 "=item The file you are trying to open 'file.xls' is in a different format than specified by the file extension."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007556 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007557 "This warning occurs when you create an XLSX file but give it an xls extension."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007558 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007559 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007560 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007561 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007562 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007563 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007564 "=head1 WRITING EXCEL FILES"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007565 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007566 "Depending on your requirements, background and general sensibilities you may prefer one of the following methods of getting data into Excel:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007567 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007568 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007569 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007570 "=item * Spreadsheet::WriteExcel"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007571 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007572 "This module is the precursor to Excel::Writer::XLSX and uses the same interface. It produces files in the Excel Biff xls format that was used in Excel versions 97-2003. These files can still be read by Excel 2007 but have some limitations in relation to the number of rows and columns that the format supports."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007573 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007574 "L<Spreadsheet::WriteExcel>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007575 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007576 "=item * Win32::OLE module and office automation"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007577 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007578 "This requires a Windows platform and an installed copy of Excel. This is the most powerful and complete method for interfacing with Excel."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007579 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007580 "L<Win32::OLE>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007581 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007582 "=item * CSV, comma separated variables or text"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007583 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007584 "Excel will open and automatically convert files with a C<csv> extension."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007585 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007586 "To create CSV files refer to the L<Text::CSV_XS> module."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007587 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007588 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007589 "=item * DBI with DBD::ADO or DBD::ODBC"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007590 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007591 "Excel files contain an internal index table that allows them to act like a database file. Using one of the standard Perl database modules you can connect to an Excel file as a database."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007592 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007593 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007594 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007595 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007596 "For other Perl-Excel modules try the following search: L<http://search.cpan.org/search?mode=module&query=excel>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007597 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007598 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007599 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007600 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007601 "=head1 READING EXCEL FILES"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007602 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007603 "To read data from Excel files try:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007604 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007605 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007606 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007607 "=item * L<Spreadsheet::ParseXLSX>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007608 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007609 "A module for reading data from XLSX files. It also imports most, if"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007610 "not all, of the metadata to be found in Excel XLSX files.  As its"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007611 "author describes it: \"This module is an adaptor for"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007612 "L<Spreadsheet::ParseExcel> that reads XLSX files. For documentation"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007613 "about the various data that you can retrieve from these classes,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007614 "please see L<Spreadsheet::ParseExcel>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007615 "L<Spreadsheet::ParseExcel::Workbook>,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007616 "L<Spreadsheet::ParseExcel::Worksheet>, and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007617 "L<Spreadsheet::ParseExcel::Cell>.\""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007618 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007619 "=item * Spreadsheet::XLSX"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007620 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007621 "A module for reading formatted or unformatted data from XLSX files."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007622 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007623 "L<Spreadsheet::XLSX>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007624 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007625 "=item * SimpleXlsx"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007626 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007627 "A lightweight module for reading data from XLSX files."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007628 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007629 "L<SimpleXlsx>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007630 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007631 "=item * Spreadsheet::ParseExcel"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007632 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007633 "This module can read data from an Excel XLS file but it doesn't support the XLSX format."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007634 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007635 "L<Spreadsheet::ParseExcel>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007636 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007637 "=item * Win32::OLE module and office automation (reading)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007638 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007639 "See above."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007640 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007641 "=item * DBI with DBD::ADO or DBD::ODBC."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007642 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007643 "See above."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007644 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007645 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007646 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007647 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007648 "For other Perl-Excel modules try the following search: L<http://search.cpan.org/search?mode=module&query=excel>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007649 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007650 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007651 "=head1 BUGS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007652 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007653 "=over"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007654 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007655 "=item * Memory usage is very high for large worksheets."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007656 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007657 "If you run out of memory creating large worksheets use the C<set_optimization()> method. See L</SPEED AND MEMORY USAGE> for more information."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007658 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007659 "=item * Perl packaging programs can't find chart modules."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007660 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007661 "When using Excel::Writer::XLSX charts with Perl packagers such as PAR or Cava you should explicitly include the chart that you are trying to create in your C<use> statements. This isn't a bug as such but it might help someone from banging their head off a wall:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007662 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007663 "    ..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007664 "    use Excel::Writer::XLSX;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007665 "    use Excel::Writer::XLSX::Chart::Column;"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007666 "    ..."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007667 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007668 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007669 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007670 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007671 "If you wish to submit a bug report run the C<bug_report.pl> program in the C<examples> directory of the distro."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007672 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007673 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007674 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007675 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007676 "The bug tracker is on Github: L<https://github.com/jmcnamara/excel-writer-xlsx/issues>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007677 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007678 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007679 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00007680 ""
